{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"8a0wvbch5MK4"},"source":["# GANA 2D Interpretability Experiment\n","\n","**Goal:** Train GANA on MNIST with `embedding_dim=2`, then visualize whether neurons that respond to similar digits cluster geometrically. If yes, this is direct evidence that the discrete curvature dynamics organize representation space meaningfully.\n","\n","**Setup:**\n","- Two network sizes: small (64 neurons, clean figure) and full (256/128, robustness check)\n","- Two response metrics: avg activation per class + selectivity index\n","- Two ablations: standard MLP with 2D bottleneck + GANA with curvature ablated\n","\n","**Hardware:** Colab T4. Run from top to bottom.\n","\n","---"],"id":"8a0wvbch5MK4"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Qv2pF5yI5MK9"},"source":["## 1. Setup"],"id":"Qv2pF5yI5MK9"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"HEghkShX5MK-","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778517451575,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":16140,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}},"outputId":"21a17c5f-cd8b-4265-d385-37aba6a969c3"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Device: cuda\n","GPU: Tesla T4\n"]}],"source":["import torch\n","import torch.nn as nn\n","import torch.nn.functional as F\n","from torch.utils.data import DataLoader, Subset\n","from torchvision import datasets, transforms\n","import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from matplotlib.colors import ListedColormap\n","import matplotlib.patches as mpatches\n","from scipy.spatial import Voronoi, voronoi_plot_2d\n","import time\n","import random\n","\n","SEED = 42\n","torch.manual_seed(SEED); np.random.seed(SEED); random.seed(SEED)\n","\n","device = torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu')\n","print(f'Device: {device}')\n","if device.type == 'cuda':\n","    print(f'GPU: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}')"],"id":"HEghkShX5MK-"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"j3oyBSC45MLB","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778517460703,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":9115,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}},"outputId":"210094d8-693e-42e1-8772-c1f9974b6df2"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["100%|██████████| 9.91M/9.91M [00:01<00:00, 5.57MB/s]\n","100%|██████████| 28.9k/28.9k [00:00<00:00, 134kB/s]\n","100%|██████████| 1.65M/1.65M [00:01<00:00, 1.24MB/s]\n","100%|██████████| 4.54k/4.54k [00:00<00:00, 12.4MB/s]"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Train: 60000, Test: 10000\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["\n"]}],"source":["# MNIST loaders\n","transform = transforms.Compose([transforms.ToTensor(), transforms.Normalize((0.1307,), (0.3081,))])\n","train_full = datasets.MNIST('./data', train=True, download=True, transform=transform)\n","test_set = datasets.MNIST('./data', train=False, download=True, transform=transform)\n","\n","# Use full training set for these experiments — interpretability matters more than data efficiency here\n","train_loader = DataLoader(train_full, batch_size=128, shuffle=True, num_workers=2, pin_memory=True)\n","test_loader = DataLoader(test_set, batch_size=512, shuffle=False, num_workers=2, pin_memory=True)\n","\n","print(f'Train: {len(train_full)}, Test: {len(test_set)}')"],"id":"j3oyBSC45MLB"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"YKuBbg9-5MLD"},"source":["## 2. Models\n","\n","Three variants share the same outer structure (input → hidden layer(s) → output). What changes is the hidden layer:\n","\n","- **GANA**: each neuron has a 2D position; activation is modulated by discrete curvature against neighbors with geometric weighting `gw=0.2`, neighbor radius `r=1.5`.\n","- **GANA-ablated**: same architecture, but curvature term zeroed (`gw=0`). Neurons still have 2D positions used for visualization, but those positions don't influence forward pass.\n","- **MLP-bottleneck**: standard MLP where the hidden layer is followed by a 2D linear bottleneck, then expanded back. Gives every \"neuron\" a 2D coordinate via the bottleneck projection.\n","\n","This matches the Phase 1 winning config (`ed=16, r=1.5, gw=0.2`) but with `ed=2`."],"id":"YKuBbg9-5MLD"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"metadata":{"id":"qnnzFo0r5MLE","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778517460715,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":17,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["class GANALayer(nn.Module):\n","    \"\"\"Single GANA layer: linear transform + curvature modulation in 2D embedding space.\"\"\"\n","    def __init__(self, in_dim, out_dim, embedding_dim=2, neighbor_radius=1.5, geom_weight=0.2):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        self.linear = nn.Linear(in_dim, out_dim)\n","        # Learnable 2D positions for each output neuron\n","        self.positions = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(out_dim, embedding_dim) * 0.5)\n","        self.neighbor_radius = neighbor_radius\n","        self.geom_weight = geom_weight\n","\n","    def compute_curvature_modulation(self, activations):\n","        # activations: (B, out_dim)\n","        # For each neuron, find neighbors within neighbor_radius and compute discrete curvature\n","        # as deviation of own activation from local neighborhood mean, weighted by inverse distance.\n","        with torch.no_grad():\n","            dists = torch.cdist(self.positions, self.positions)  # (out_dim, out_dim)\n","            mask = (dists < self.neighbor_radius) & (dists > 1e-6)  # exclude self\n","            inv_dist = torch.where(mask, 1.0 / (dists + 1e-6), torch.zeros_like(dists))\n","            row_sum = inv_dist.sum(dim=1, keepdim=True).clamp(min=1e-6)\n","            weights = inv_dist / row_sum  # (out_dim, out_dim) row-stochastic over neighbors\n","        # Local mean activation per neuron from its neighbors: (B, out_dim)\n","        local_mean = activations @ weights.t()\n","        # Curvature = own activation - local mean. Modulation pulls activations slightly toward consistency.\n","        curvature = activations - local_mean\n","        return activations - self.geom_weight * curvature\n","\n","    def forward(self, x):\n","        a = self.linear(x)\n","        if self.geom_weight > 0:\n","            a = self.compute_curvature_modulation(a)\n","        return F.relu(a)\n","\n","\n","class GANAModel(nn.Module):\n","    def __init__(self, hidden_dims, num_classes=10, embedding_dim=2, neighbor_radius=1.5, geom_weight=0.2):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        layers = []\n","        in_dim = 28 * 28\n","        for h in hidden_dims:\n","            layers.append(GANALayer(in_dim, h, embedding_dim, neighbor_radius, geom_weight))\n","            in_dim = h\n","        self.hidden = nn.ModuleList(layers)\n","        self.classifier = nn.Linear(in_dim, num_classes)\n","\n","    def forward(self, x, return_activations=False):\n","        x = x.view(x.size(0), -1)\n","        acts = []\n","        for layer in self.hidden:\n","            x = layer(x)\n","            acts.append(x)\n","        logits = self.classifier(x)\n","        if return_activations:\n","            return logits, acts\n","        return logits\n","\n","\n","class MLPBottleneckModel(nn.Module):\n","    \"\"\"Standard MLP where hidden activations are projected through a 2D bottleneck.\n","    The bottleneck weight matrix gives each neuron a 2D coordinate (its column in the projection).\"\"\"\n","    def __init__(self, hidden_dims, num_classes=10, bottleneck_dim=2):\n","        super().__init__()\n","        layers = []\n","        in_dim = 28 * 28\n","        for h in hidden_dims:\n","            layers.append(nn.Linear(in_dim, h))\n","            layers.append(nn.ReLU())\n","            in_dim = h\n","        self.hidden = nn.Sequential(*layers)\n","        # Bottleneck: project last hidden dim to 2D, then back\n","        self.to_2d = nn.Linear(in_dim, bottleneck_dim, bias=False)\n","        self.from_2d = nn.Linear(bottleneck_dim, in_dim)\n","        self.classifier = nn.Linear(in_dim, num_classes)\n","        self.last_hidden_dim = in_dim\n","\n","    def forward(self, x, return_activations=False):\n","        x = x.view(x.size(0), -1)\n","        h = self.hidden(x)\n","        z = self.to_2d(h)\n","        h2 = F.relu(self.from_2d(z))\n","        logits = self.classifier(h2)\n","        if return_activations:\n","            return logits, [h2]\n","        return logits\n","\n","    def get_neuron_positions(self):\n","        # For the last hidden layer's neurons, position = column of from_2d weight (1 row per 2D coord -> per-neuron 2D pos)\n","        # from_2d weight shape: (last_hidden_dim, 2). Each row = that neuron's 2D position.\n","        return self.from_2d.weight.detach().cpu().numpy()"],"id":"qnnzFo0r5MLE"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"eFT5Aq375MLG"},"source":["## 3. Training utilities"],"id":"eFT5Aq375MLG"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"metadata":{"id":"JZGVIclk5MLH","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778517460781,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":30,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["def train_model(model, train_loader, test_loader, epochs=10, lr=1e-3, label='model'):\n","    model = model.to(device)\n","    opt = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=lr)\n","    sched = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR(opt, T_max=epochs)\n","    history = {'train_loss': [], 'test_acc': []}\n","\n","    for ep in range(epochs):\n","        model.train()\n","        running = 0.0\n","        n = 0\n","        t0 = time.time()\n","        for x, y in train_loader:\n","            x, y = x.to(device, non_blocking=True), y.to(device, non_blocking=True)\n","            opt.zero_grad()\n","            logits = model(x)\n","            loss = F.cross_entropy(logits, y)\n","            loss.backward()\n","            opt.step()\n","            running += loss.item() * x.size(0)\n","            n += x.size(0)\n","        sched.step()\n","\n","        # Eval\n","        model.eval()\n","        correct = 0; total = 0\n","        with torch.no_grad():\n","            for x, y in test_loader:\n","                x, y = x.to(device), y.to(device)\n","                pred = model(x).argmax(1)\n","                correct += (pred == y).sum().item()\n","                total += y.size(0)\n","        acc = correct / total\n","        history['train_loss'].append(running / n)\n","        history['test_acc'].append(acc)\n","        print(f'[{label}] ep {ep+1}/{epochs}  loss={running/n:.4f}  test_acc={acc:.4f}  ({time.time()-t0:.1f}s)')\n","    return history\n","\n","\n","def collect_neuron_responses(model, loader, layer_idx=-1):\n","    \"\"\"For each test sample, get the activations of the chosen hidden layer.\n","    Returns: activations (N, num_neurons), labels (N,).\"\"\"\n","    model.eval()\n","    all_acts, all_y = [], []\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for x, y in loader:\n","            x = x.to(device)\n","            _, acts = model(x, return_activations=True)\n","            all_acts.append(acts[layer_idx].cpu())\n","            all_y.append(y)\n","    return torch.cat(all_acts).numpy(), torch.cat(all_y).numpy()\n","\n","\n","def class_response_metrics(activations, labels, num_classes=10):\n","    \"\"\"Returns:\n","      avg_act: (num_neurons, num_classes) — mean activation of each neuron per class\n","      preferred_class: (num_neurons,) — argmax class\n","      selectivity: (num_neurons,) — (top - mean of rest) / (top + mean of rest)\n","    \"\"\"\n","    num_neurons = activations.shape[1]\n","    avg_act = np.zeros((num_neurons, num_classes))\n","    for c in range(num_classes):\n","        mask = labels == c\n","        if mask.sum() > 0:\n","            avg_act[:, c] = activations[mask].mean(axis=0)\n","    preferred = avg_act.argmax(axis=1)\n","    top = avg_act.max(axis=1)\n","    rest_mean = (avg_act.sum(axis=1) - top) / (num_classes - 1)\n","    selectivity = (top - rest_mean) / (top + rest_mean + 1e-8)\n","    return avg_act, preferred, selectivity"],"id":"JZGVIclk5MLH"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"lppVanfK5MLJ"},"source":["## 4. Train all six models\n","\n","(2 sizes) × (3 variants) = 6 runs. Small models train in ~2 min each, full in ~5 min each. Total ~25 min on T4."],"id":"lppVanfK5MLJ"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"tOb1Y0vu5MLK","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778518287991,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":827202,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}},"outputId":"72e0905b-48c0-47a8-a6ca-a88fb5050aeb"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["\n","=== Training small_gana ===\n","[small_gana] ep 1/10  loss=0.3672  test_acc=0.9380  (14.8s)\n","[small_gana] ep 2/10  loss=0.1750  test_acc=0.9578  (14.1s)\n","[small_gana] ep 3/10  loss=0.1269  test_acc=0.9665  (14.5s)\n","[small_gana] ep 4/10  loss=0.1003  test_acc=0.9697  (15.0s)\n","[small_gana] ep 5/10  loss=0.0832  test_acc=0.9734  (14.0s)\n","[small_gana] ep 6/10  loss=0.0709  test_acc=0.9743  (14.3s)\n","[small_gana] ep 7/10  loss=0.0620  test_acc=0.9749  (14.3s)\n","[small_gana] ep 8/10  loss=0.0557  test_acc=0.9753  (14.6s)\n","[small_gana] ep 9/10  loss=0.0518  test_acc=0.9766  (14.4s)\n","[small_gana] ep 10/10  loss=0.0495  test_acc=0.9767  (14.2s)\n","\n","=== Training small_gana_abl ===\n","[small_gana_abl] ep 1/10  loss=0.3500  test_acc=0.9445  (13.6s)\n","[small_gana_abl] ep 2/10  loss=0.1651  test_acc=0.9602  (13.6s)\n","[small_gana_abl] ep 3/10  loss=0.1198  test_acc=0.9678  (13.5s)\n","[small_gana_abl] ep 4/10  loss=0.0948  test_acc=0.9694  (13.6s)\n","[small_gana_abl] ep 5/10  loss=0.0787  test_acc=0.9725  (13.5s)\n","[small_gana_abl] ep 6/10  loss=0.0669  test_acc=0.9743  (13.4s)\n","[small_gana_abl] ep 7/10  loss=0.0585  test_acc=0.9758  (13.5s)\n","[small_gana_abl] ep 8/10  loss=0.0521  test_acc=0.9761  (13.6s)\n","[small_gana_abl] ep 9/10  loss=0.0482  test_acc=0.9770  (13.3s)\n","[small_gana_abl] ep 10/10  loss=0.0459  test_acc=0.9772  (13.3s)\n","\n","=== Training small_mlp_bn ===\n","[small_mlp_bn] ep 1/10  loss=0.8357  test_acc=0.8355  (13.4s)\n","[small_mlp_bn] ep 2/10  loss=0.4326  test_acc=0.8951  (13.4s)\n","[small_mlp_bn] ep 3/10  loss=0.3155  test_acc=0.9123  (13.4s)\n","[small_mlp_bn] ep 4/10  loss=0.2599  test_acc=0.9266  (13.4s)\n","[small_mlp_bn] ep 5/10  loss=0.2240  test_acc=0.9294  (13.3s)\n","[small_mlp_bn] ep 6/10  loss=0.1963  test_acc=0.9322  (13.5s)\n","[small_mlp_bn] ep 7/10  loss=0.1780  test_acc=0.9361  (13.9s)\n","[small_mlp_bn] ep 8/10  loss=0.1623  test_acc=0.9366  (13.6s)\n","[small_mlp_bn] ep 9/10  loss=0.1531  test_acc=0.9391  (13.7s)\n","[small_mlp_bn] ep 10/10  loss=0.1475  test_acc=0.9385  (13.5s)\n","\n","=== Training full_gana ===\n","[full_gana] ep 1/10  loss=0.2940  test_acc=0.9596  (14.0s)\n","[full_gana] ep 2/10  loss=0.1104  test_acc=0.9715  (14.1s)\n","[full_gana] ep 3/10  loss=0.0723  test_acc=0.9712  (13.8s)\n","[full_gana] ep 4/10  loss=0.0484  test_acc=0.9767  (14.0s)\n","[full_gana] ep 5/10  loss=0.0346  test_acc=0.9788  (14.3s)\n","[full_gana] ep 6/10  loss=0.0218  test_acc=0.9797  (14.2s)\n","[full_gana] ep 7/10  loss=0.0136  test_acc=0.9809  (14.4s)\n","[full_gana] ep 8/10  loss=0.0087  test_acc=0.9820  (14.2s)\n","[full_gana] ep 9/10  loss=0.0063  test_acc=0.9821  (15.3s)\n","[full_gana] ep 10/10  loss=0.0051  test_acc=0.9822  (14.3s)\n","\n","=== Training full_gana_abl ===\n","[full_gana_abl] ep 1/10  loss=0.2703  test_acc=0.9633  (13.6s)\n","[full_gana_abl] ep 2/10  loss=0.1020  test_acc=0.9715  (14.0s)\n","[full_gana_abl] ep 3/10  loss=0.0681  test_acc=0.9731  (13.8s)\n","[full_gana_abl] ep 4/10  loss=0.0453  test_acc=0.9784  (13.5s)\n","[full_gana_abl] ep 5/10  loss=0.0313  test_acc=0.9809  (13.4s)\n","[full_gana_abl] ep 6/10  loss=0.0196  test_acc=0.9818  (13.4s)\n","[full_gana_abl] ep 7/10  loss=0.0112  test_acc=0.9821  (13.2s)\n","[full_gana_abl] ep 8/10  loss=0.0068  test_acc=0.9830  (13.4s)\n","[full_gana_abl] ep 9/10  loss=0.0047  test_acc=0.9835  (13.4s)\n","[full_gana_abl] ep 10/10  loss=0.0038  test_acc=0.9834  (13.2s)\n","\n","=== Training full_mlp_bn ===\n","[full_mlp_bn] ep 1/10  loss=0.5697  test_acc=0.9174  (13.2s)\n","[full_mlp_bn] ep 2/10  loss=0.2143  test_acc=0.9486  (13.2s)\n","[full_mlp_bn] ep 3/10  loss=0.1490  test_acc=0.9558  (13.5s)\n","[full_mlp_bn] ep 4/10  loss=0.1090  test_acc=0.9613  (13.6s)\n","[full_mlp_bn] ep 5/10  loss=0.0824  test_acc=0.9612  (13.5s)\n","[full_mlp_bn] ep 6/10  loss=0.0615  test_acc=0.9650  (13.4s)\n","[full_mlp_bn] ep 7/10  loss=0.0444  test_acc=0.9668  (13.6s)\n","[full_mlp_bn] ep 8/10  loss=0.0329  test_acc=0.9684  (13.9s)\n","[full_mlp_bn] ep 9/10  loss=0.0255  test_acc=0.9698  (13.6s)\n","[full_mlp_bn] ep 10/10  loss=0.0213  test_acc=0.9703  (13.8s)\n","\n","=== Final test accuracies ===\n","  small_gana           0.9767\n","  small_gana_abl       0.9772\n","  small_mlp_bn         0.9385\n","  full_gana            0.9822\n","  full_gana_abl        0.9834\n","  full_mlp_bn          0.9703\n"]}],"source":["EPOCHS = 10\n","results = {}\n","\n","configs = {\n","    'small_gana':       {'hidden': [64],       'cls': GANAModel,           'kw': {'embedding_dim': 2, 'neighbor_radius': 1.5, 'geom_weight': 0.2}},\n","    'small_gana_abl':   {'hidden': [64],       'cls': GANAModel,           'kw': {'embedding_dim': 2, 'neighbor_radius': 1.5, 'geom_weight': 0.0}},\n","    'small_mlp_bn':     {'hidden': [64],       'cls': MLPBottleneckModel,  'kw': {'bottleneck_dim': 2}},\n","    'full_gana':        {'hidden': [256, 128], 'cls': GANAModel,           'kw': {'embedding_dim': 2, 'neighbor_radius': 1.5, 'geom_weight': 0.2}},\n","    'full_gana_abl':    {'hidden': [256, 128], 'cls': GANAModel,           'kw': {'embedding_dim': 2, 'neighbor_radius': 1.5, 'geom_weight': 0.0}},\n","    'full_mlp_bn':      {'hidden': [256, 128], 'cls': MLPBottleneckModel,  'kw': {'bottleneck_dim': 2}},\n","}\n","\n","for name, cfg in configs.items():\n","    print(f'\\n=== Training {name} ===')\n","    torch.manual_seed(SEED)  # same init seed across variants for fair-ish comparison\n","    model = cfg['cls'](cfg['hidden'], **cfg['kw'])\n","    hist = train_model(model, train_loader, test_loader, epochs=EPOCHS, label=name)\n","    results[name] = {'model': model, 'history': hist, 'config': cfg}\n","\n","print('\\n=== Final test accuracies ===')\n","for name in configs:\n","    print(f'  {name:20s} {results[name][\"history\"][\"test_acc\"][-1]:.4f}')"],"id":"tOb1Y0vu5MLK"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"pbOmt0KL5MLM"},"source":["## 5. Extract positions and responses"],"id":"pbOmt0KL5MLM"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"3NiSkm5_5MLM","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778518298068,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":10065,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}},"outputId":"1b2bbe66-572d-4373-cd0b-b1deea6d7c52"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["small_gana            neurons=  64  mean_selectivity=0.504  active_neurons=64\n","small_gana_abl        neurons=  64  mean_selectivity=0.489  active_neurons=60\n","small_mlp_bn          neurons=  64  mean_selectivity=0.664  active_neurons=64\n","full_gana             neurons= 128  mean_selectivity=0.506  active_neurons=128\n","full_gana_abl         neurons= 128  mean_selectivity=0.511  active_neurons=121\n","full_mlp_bn           neurons= 128  mean_selectivity=0.654  active_neurons=127\n"]}],"source":["def extract_neuron_data(name, results):\n","    \"\"\"Returns (positions, avg_act, preferred, selectivity) for the LAST hidden layer.\"\"\"\n","    model = results[name]['model']\n","    activations, labels = collect_neuron_responses(model, test_loader, layer_idx=-1)\n","    avg_act, pref, sel = class_response_metrics(activations, labels)\n","\n","    if isinstance(model, GANAModel):\n","        pos = model.hidden[-1].positions.detach().cpu().numpy()\n","    else:\n","        pos = model.get_neuron_positions()\n","    return pos, avg_act, pref, sel\n","\n","neuron_data = {name: extract_neuron_data(name, results) for name in configs}\n","for name, (pos, _, pref, sel) in neuron_data.items():\n","    print(f'{name:20s}  neurons={pos.shape[0]:4d}  mean_selectivity={sel.mean():.3f}  active_neurons={(sel > 0.1).sum()}')"],"id":"3NiSkm5_5MLM"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"JwlsBuAw5MLN"},"source":["## 6. Main figure: 2D neuron maps colored by preferred class\n","\n","This is the money shot. If GANA's geometry is meaningful, neurons preferring similar digits should cluster spatially. Ablation and MLP-bottleneck should look more random."],"id":"JwlsBuAw5MLN"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":311},"id":"4fLJnnd75MLO","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778518301030,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":2956,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}},"outputId":"07c6ca98-175d-42b3-c64e-3e780ff2b98f"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x900 with 6 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["DIGIT_COLORS = plt.cm.tab10(np.arange(10))\n","\n","def plot_neuron_map(ax, pos, pref, sel, title, alpha_min=0.2):\n","    # Selectivity drives marker alpha — neurons that don't strongly prefer anything fade.\n","    sel_norm = (sel - sel.min()) / (sel.max() - sel.min() + 1e-8)\n","    sel_norm = alpha_min + (1 - alpha_min) * sel_norm\n","    sizes = 30 + 200 * sel_norm\n","    for c in range(10):\n","        mask = pref == c\n","        if mask.sum() == 0:\n","            continue\n","        ax.scatter(pos[mask, 0], pos[mask, 1],\n","                   c=[DIGIT_COLORS[c]], s=sizes[mask], alpha=sel_norm[mask],\n","                   edgecolors='white', linewidths=0.5, label=str(c))\n","    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=11)\n","    ax.set_xticks([]); ax.set_yticks([])\n","    ax.set_aspect('equal', adjustable='datalim')\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 3, figsize=(14, 9))\n","panel_order = [\n","    ('small_gana',     'Small GANA (geom_weight=0.2)'),\n","    ('small_gana_abl', 'Small GANA-ablated (geom_weight=0)'),\n","    ('small_mlp_bn',   'Small MLP + 2D bottleneck'),\n","    ('full_gana',      'Full GANA (256/128)'),\n","    ('full_gana_abl',  'Full GANA-ablated'),\n","    ('full_mlp_bn',    'Full MLP + 2D bottleneck'),\n","]\n","for ax, (name, title) in zip(axes.flat, panel_order):\n","    pos, _, pref, sel = neuron_data[name]\n","    acc = results[name]['history']['test_acc'][-1]\n","    plot_neuron_map(ax, pos, pref, sel, f'{title}\\nacc={acc:.3f}')\n","\n","# Shared legend\n","handles = [mpatches.Patch(color=DIGIT_COLORS[c], label=f'digit {c}') for c in range(10)]\n","fig.legend(handles=handles, loc='lower center', ncol=10, frameon=False, bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.02))\n","fig.suptitle('Neuron 2D positions, colored by preferred digit class\\n(opacity & size ∝ class selectivity)', fontsize=13)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig('fig_2d_neuron_maps.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n","plt.show()"],"id":"4fLJnnd75MLO"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"hUiMP5Wi5MLP"},"source":["## 7. Quantifying \"clustering\" — is the structure real?\n","\n","Eyeballing isn't proof. Compute, for each model, a **spatial-class coherence score**: for each neuron, what fraction of its k nearest spatial neighbors share its preferred class? Higher = more geometric structure. Compare to a shuffled baseline."],"id":"hUiMP5Wi5MLP"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":8,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"8_FVb2Uq5MLQ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778518301300,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":262,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}},"outputId":"865e9b2a-5ff5-47f0-ff74-2276821dd964"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Model                    Coherence   Shuffle μ   Shuffle σ   Z-score\n","--------------------------------------------------------------------\n","small_gana                  0.1406      0.1077      0.0207      1.59\n","small_gana_abl              0.0719      0.0972      0.0220     -1.15\n","small_mlp_bn                0.6969      0.1320      0.0229     24.67\n","full_gana                   0.1297      0.1102      0.0152      1.28\n","full_gana_abl               0.1406      0.1212      0.0162      1.20\n","full_mlp_bn                 0.8578      0.1730      0.0197     34.83\n"]}],"source":["from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n","\n","def spatial_coherence(pos, pref, k=5, n_shuffles=100):\n","    \"\"\"For each neuron, fraction of k nearest spatial neighbors that share preferred class.\n","    Returns (mean_coherence, shuffle_mean, shuffle_std, z_score).\"\"\"\n","    n = len(pos)\n","    k = min(k, n - 1)\n","    nn_model = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k + 1).fit(pos)  # +1 because self is included\n","    _, idx = nn_model.kneighbors(pos)\n","    idx = idx[:, 1:]  # drop self\n","    same = (pref[idx] == pref[:, None]).mean()\n","    # Shuffle baseline: randomize preferred labels, recompute\n","    shuffle_scores = []\n","    rng = np.random.default_rng(SEED)\n","    for _ in range(n_shuffles):\n","        shuffled = rng.permutation(pref)\n","        shuffle_scores.append((shuffled[idx] == shuffled[:, None]).mean())\n","    shuffle_scores = np.array(shuffle_scores)\n","    z = (same - shuffle_scores.mean()) / (shuffle_scores.std() + 1e-8)\n","    return same, shuffle_scores.mean(), shuffle_scores.std(), z\n","\n","print(f'{\"Model\":<22}{\"Coherence\":>12}{\"Shuffle μ\":>12}{\"Shuffle σ\":>12}{\"Z-score\":>10}')\n","print('-' * 68)\n","coherence_table = {}\n","for name in configs:\n","    pos, _, pref, _ = neuron_data[name]\n","    c, sm, ss, z = spatial_coherence(pos, pref, k=5)\n","    coherence_table[name] = (c, sm, ss, z)\n","    print(f'{name:<22}{c:>12.4f}{sm:>12.4f}{ss:>12.4f}{z:>10.2f}')"],"id":"8_FVb2Uq5MLQ"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"YqlZMHXv5MLQ"},"source":["**Reading the table:** Z-score > 2 means the spatial-class clustering is significantly better than random. The headline result for the paper is the gap between `gana` and `gana_abl` rows — same architecture, only the curvature term differs."],"id":"YqlZMHXv5MLQ"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"zufm7izU5MLR"},"source":["## 8. Supplementary: selectivity distributions\n","\n","How sharp are the neurons' class preferences?"],"id":"zufm7izU5MLR"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":9,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":164},"id":"teeFcmUy5MLS","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778518302085,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":764,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}},"outputId":"7a44ce22-d055-4355-9806-ed2c5347ec5b"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x400 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n","for ax, size in zip(axes, ['small', 'full']):\n","    for variant, color in zip(['gana', 'gana_abl', 'mlp_bn'], ['C0', 'C1', 'C2']):\n","        name = f'{size}_{variant}'\n","        _, _, _, sel = neuron_data[name]\n","        ax.hist(sel, bins=30, alpha=0.5, label=variant, color=color, density=True)\n","    ax.set_title(f'{size.capitalize()} models — selectivity distribution')\n","    ax.set_xlabel('Selectivity index')\n","    ax.set_ylabel('Density')\n","    ax.legend()\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig('fig_selectivity_dist.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n","plt.show()"],"id":"teeFcmUy5MLS"},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"G9fMm5_K5MLS"},"source":["## 9. Supplementary: per-class activation heatmaps\n","\n","For the small_gana model, show which neurons (sorted by spatial position angle) respond to which class. Reveals whether digits occupy distinct angular sectors of the embedding plane."],"id":"G9fMm5_K5MLS"},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":10,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":730},"id":"NWxhVXzf5MLT","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778518303932,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":1841,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}},"outputId":"ea4a6b90-39d4-4f0b-cebb-4049c1fd6eae"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x500 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x500 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x500 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["def plot_response_heatmap(name):\n","    pos, avg_act, pref, sel = neuron_data[name]\n","    # Sort neurons by angle in 2D plane\n","    angles = np.arctan2(pos[:, 1], pos[:, 0])\n","    order = np.argsort(angles)\n","    avg_norm = avg_act / (avg_act.max(axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-8)\n","    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 5))\n","    im = ax.imshow(avg_norm[order].T, aspect='auto', cmap='viridis')\n","    ax.set_yticks(range(10)); ax.set_yticklabels([f'digit {c}' for c in range(10)])\n","    ax.set_xlabel('Neuron index (sorted by angular position)')\n","    ax.set_title(f'{name}: per-class activation (row-normalized)')\n","    plt.colorbar(im, ax=ax, label='normalized activation')\n","    plt.tight_layout()\n","    plt.savefig(f'fig_heatmap_{name}.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","plot_response_heatmap('small_gana')\n","plot_response_heatmap('small_gana_abl')\n","plot_response_heatmap('small_mlp_bn')"],"id":"NWxhVXzf5MLT"},{"cell_type":"code","source":["!zip results.zip fig_*.png gana_2d_results.json\n","from google.colab import files\n","files.download('results.zip')"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":141},"id":"Ka0PFVLF-UVL","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778518683856,"user_tz":-60,"elapsed":164,"user":{"displayName":"Oyewole Emmanuel","userId":"16142686126501812905"}},"outputId":"227414ec-9406-42a3-d3d3-ccf2e37317e7"},"id":"Ka0PFVLF-UVL","execution_count":12,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["  adding: fig_2d_neuron_maps.png (deflated 3%)\n","  adding: fig_heatmap_small_gana_abl.png (deflated 19%)\n","  adding: fig_heatmap_small_gana.png (deflated 19%)\n","  adding: fig_heatmap_small_mlp_bn.png (deflated 19%)\n","  adding: fig_selectivity_dist.png (deflated 20%)\n","  adding: gana_2d_results.json (deflated 69%)\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<IPython.core.display.Javascript object>"],"application/javascript":["\n","    async function download(id, filename, size) {\n","      if (!google.colab.kernel.accessAllowed) {\n","        return;\n","      }\n","      const div = document.createElement('div');\n","      const label = document.createElement('label');\n","      label.textContent = `Downloading \"${filename}\": `;\n","      div.appendChild(label);\n","      const progress = document.createElement('progress');\n","      progress.max = size;\n","      div.appendChild(progress);\n","      document.body.appendChild(div);\n","\n","      const buffers = [];\n","      let downloaded = 0;\n","\n","      const channel = await google.colab.kernel.comms.open(id);\n","      // Send a message to notify the kernel that we're ready.\n","      channel.send({})\n","\n","      for await (const message of channel.messages) {\n","        // Send a message to notify the kernel that we're ready.\n","        channel.send({})\n","        if (message.buffer